    {
      "id": "59ce1d05-f59e-47ce-8912-56d0f3176e21",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualization of Group Statistics by using Boxplots",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "b2043fcd-04c4-479d-9920-415a89d256aa",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ggplot(df, aes(x = region4, y = gnipc)) +\n  geom_boxplot(alpha = 0.7,                    # Transparency \n               fill = \"steelblue\") +           # Fill color\n  labs(title = \"Comparison of Gross Regional Product per capita across Regions in China 2024\",\n       x = \"Region\",\n       y = \"GRP Value (10,000 CNY)\",\n       caption = \"Data Source: National Bureau of Statistics of China\") +\n  theme_minimal() +\n  theme(legend.position = \"none\")              # Remove legend (redundant here)",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "9de019b8-91ff-47d1-ada3-88a6d4511dd1",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualization of Group Statistics by using Means and Standard Deviations\n\n",
      "metadata": {},
      "attachments": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "680081df-8ef1-4099-a974-5c4cfff35840",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "\n# We have to calculate the parameters first and save the group values as new variables\n# NOTE: You don't have to fully understand the coding, no worries. :)\ntmean = by(gnipc, region4, mean) # compute group means\ntsd = by(gnipc, region4, sd) # compute standard deviations of groups\n# Merge both parameter sets into a new data set\ndf_means = data.frame(tmean, tsd) # create data set \ndf_means$region = rownames(df_means) # add region labels\n\n# Create the chart\nggplot(df_means, aes(x=region, y=tmean)) + \n  geom_errorbar(aes(ymin = tmean-tsd, ymax = tmean+tsd), width=0.01, color=\"steelblue\") +\n  geom_point(color=\"darkblue\", size=3) + \n  labs(title = \"Comparison of Gross Regional Product across Regions in China\",\n       x = \"Region\",\n       y = \"GRP Value (10,000 CNY)\",\n       caption = \"Data Source: National Bureau of Statistics of China\") +\n  theme_minimal()                         # A clean, popular theme\n\n",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "43a0731f-33fd-49b9-98e7-3bb226c73940",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualization of the association between two metric variables",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "356eabba-2047-476d-b629-0a983ae1baa7",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ggplot(df, aes(x = grp2, y = grp3)) +        # Define axes\n  geom_point(alpha = 0.7,                    # Transparency of points\n             color = \"steelblue\") +          # Color of points\n  labs(title = \"Association of GRP in Secondary and Tertiary Sector\",\n       subtitle = \"10,000 CNY\",\n       x = \"GRP II. Sector (Industry)\",\n       y = \"GRP III. Sector (Services)\",\n       caption = \"Data Source: National Bureau of Statistics of China\") +\n  theme_minimal() +\n  theme(legend.position = \"none\")           # Remove legend",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "184ee857-0e9b-4849-9a5d-0602fee5896a",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## **Additional techniques**",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "1d5248f3-088f-451b-8592-38c0f5a2897e",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Outlier analysis",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "e026401a-a1b5-4a78-8ee4-f5c019d50378",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "province[grp3 > 38000 & grp2 < 20000]",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "8700485e-c568-482e-9d01-76a00a250a35",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Regression analysis",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "8f67c4b1-9865-4a3c-a133-342bb37d3715",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "lm(grp3 ~ grp2)\n# on average, we observe additional 55,920 CNY \n# gain in services productivity for each increase \n# of primary sector poductivity by 10,000 CNY  ",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "c5517e30-e9eb-4971-9cb6-d106c83b9be7",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "lm(grp3 ~ grp2, data=df[!(grp3 > 38000 & grp2 < 20000),])\n# There is no big change in output if outliers are excuded",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "ba358ea1-b57f-4f6d-bb49-f686e6934d95",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualization of regression line",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "8ca942d2-3a7a-4075-b950-77505d1f16bb",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "\nggplot(df, aes(x = grp2, y = grp3)) +        \n  geom_point(alpha = 0.7,                    \n             color = \"steelblue\") +          \n  geom_smooth(method = \"lm\", formula = y ~ x, se = F, color = \"darkblue\") +  # regression line added\n  labs(title = \"Association of GRP in Secondary and Tertiary Sector\",\n       subtitle = \"10,000 CNY\",\n       x = \"GRP II. Sector (Industry)\",\n       y = \"GRP III. Sector (Services)\",\n       caption = \"Data Source: National Bureau of Statistics of China\") +\n  theme_minimal() +\n  theme(legend.position = \"none\")           # Remove legend",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 41
    },
    {
